!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/an-enum-over-a-family-that-is-no-identifier-family-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4"
  description: """
    An enum's members are names, equal only to themselves under their type's equality, and its
    `name_type` must be an identifier family -- an atom-family instance whose constructor IS-A
    `identifier_type`. So `name_type: integer` is refused at schema load. A numeric value set is `integer`'s own `members` facet
    (`!integer ^ { members: [80 443] }`), where `80` and `0x50` are one member; as labels they would
    be two.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
